{
  "abstract": "Over half of the known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. We invert this elimination by parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$, where the regular fifths become linear in the trace $S_{ab}$ and all three remaining conditions complete the square in $S_{ab}$. Vanishing of their discriminants cuts out two families of sextuple and $19/21$ septuple surfaces: the Branch-1 surface $E_{Br1}$ and the twin-fifth surfaces $E_{F1}, E_{F3}$. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and a new rational almost septuple $S_7^{(20/21)}$ of relation type $(5,2)$. Factoring the four-variable regular relation on the fifths defines $S_{4,2}$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. In $(r,\\mu,z)$ and Lorentz $(r,u,v,\\theta)$ coordinates, we establish the One-$R_5$ Dual Brahmagupta blow-up $P_{blowup}=0$ and Two-Conic surface $P_{surf}=0$ covering $N_{core}=0$ ($4:1$), classify sub-regular and collision curves (including the genus-five slice $F_{12}=0$ and a $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{133})$ almost septuple), and prove a $2$-adic lock on $E_B$ and rank-zero descent on $E_{16}$. Finally, we establish $3$-torsion Master Syzygies closing $C_{triad}$ and $H=1/3$, paired/antipodal source closures, the Monomial Fifth Law, and the Bi-Euler $9$-tuple $U_9^{biEuler}(r,t)$ in a free rank-three $\\mathbb{Z}[r]$-module $M_3$ with $21/36$ squares, $15$ $r$-only shifts, and a genus-four coincidence curve $C_{coinc,r}$. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Version 22 implements all four minor editorial recommendations from the Version 21 referee report (splitting Theorem 4(1)(c) into (c1)-(c3) and splitting the final bullet of Theorem 7(6); stating the generic 4:1 reconstruction domain U and generic relation types explicitly in Theorem 4(1)(c1); removing 'Unramified' from Item 9's heading in THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md and noting the 4 simple branch points at U=+/-1; synchronizing euler_sixth_entry in exp63, clarifying exp62 Part 3, and making the abstract conceptual rather than a symbol catalogue) and adds Theorem 20(51)-(59) (Items 23-25 in THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md, verified in exp64-exp66): (1) unconditional Case-A collision closure 4*r*t*(t^2-1)*(g_{Euler,+} - f_{a,-}) = 4*t^2*(X_2^2 - X_1^2 - (4*r^2-1)) = P_{CaseA}(r,t^2), the t-only shift for 1+b*f_{b,-}, the involution iota_t : t -> -1/t, Three-Way Pythagorean Conservation Laws linking Q_I, Q_II, Q_III, Universal Euler Biquadratic Addition Law and Level-2 Mordell-Weil towers Q_{5,(2,eps)}^{refl}(r), and the Coincidence Dichotomy splitting R_4(a,d_-,f_{a,-},g_{Euler,+})=0 into t=+/-t_1(r) (g=0) and the smooth g=4 curve C_{coinc,r} (r^2=(Y-2*X-4)*(Y+2*X-4)/(64*(X+4)), t=-4/X) over E_{coinc} : Y^2 = X^3+8*X^2+32*X+80 where Q_I, Q_II = square by Hilbert 90 (exp64); (2) the Universal Euler 7-Tuple S_7^{Euler,c}(r,t) (15/21 squares, 6 r-only shifts), the 28-pair algebra of U_8^{Euler}(r,t) (18/28 squares, 20/28 on t_1(r)), and the Universal Monomial Fifth Theorem e_{reg}(x,y,z,d_-) = -4*r*s*t*r_x*r_y*r_z/(x*y*z*d_- - 1)^2 yielding 15 rational 18/21 septuple extensions of S_6^{refl}(r) (exp65); and (3) the Universal Bi-Euler 9-Tuple U_9^{bi-Euler}(r,t) (21/36 squares, 23/36 on t_1(r) and C_{coinc}) with all 15 open pairs having r-only shifts, the free rank-3 Z[r]-module M_3 = Z[r]*a + Z[r]*b + Z[r]*r_{a,d_-}, the Jump-Product Shift Law, Zero-Sum Triangle Laws, unit-off-diagonal Lorentz boosts, Root-Sum Laws, and the osculating section t_{III}(r) on E_{III}(r) giving 22/36 squares (exp66).",
